<GuidePage
  title="Healthcare & the NHS in London"
  description="How to access healthcare as a new arrival in London — registering with a GP, using the NHS, understanding what's free, dental care, mental health support and private options."
  category="The Anchor"
  categoryHref="/anchor"
  heroBg="var(--terracotta-pale)"
  readTime="7 min"
  lastUpdated="May 2026"
  mascotSrc="/mascots/anchor-healthcare.png"
>

  <p>
    The NHS (National Health Service) is one of the most remarkable things about living in the
    UK — most healthcare is free at the point of use. As someone who has paid the Immigration
    Health Surcharge (IHS) as part of your visa, or who is otherwise entitled to NHS care, you
    have full access. But knowing <em>how</em> to use it is the bit that takes some getting
    used to.
  </p>

  <!-- ── Register with a GP ─────────────── -->
  <h2>Step one: register with a GP</h2>

  <p>
    A GP (General Practitioner) is your family doctor — your first point of contact for
    almost everything health-related. You cannot simply turn up at a GP surgery as a new
    patient; you need to <strong>register first</strong>, and this should be one of your
    first tasks after arriving.
  </p>

  <p>How to do it:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Go to <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/service-search/find-a-gp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nhs.uk/find-a-gp</a> and search by postcode</li>
    <li>Check the surgery is accepting new patients — not all are, especially in busy areas</li>
    <li>Register online (most now accept online registration) or visit in person</li>
    <li>You'll need your name, date of birth, address, and NHS number if you have one — but you don't need an NHS number to register</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="callout callout--tip">
    <span class="callout__heading">✦ Tip</span>
    <p>
      Register with a GP as soon as you have a permanent address — there are often waiting
      lists, and you'll want to be registered <em>before</em> you need them. If your local
      surgery isn't accepting patients, you have the right to register at any GP within
      a reasonable distance, even outside your immediate area.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- ── NHS app ───────────────────────── -->
  <h2>The NHS app</h2>

  <p>
    Download it. It's genuinely useful. Once registered with a GP, you can use the NHS app to:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Book and manage GP appointments</li>
    <li>View your medical records and test results</li>
    <li>Order repeat prescriptions</li>
    <li>Access your vaccination history and COVID records</li>
    <li>Get 111 online advice</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="partner-grid">
    <PartnerCard
      name="NHS App"
